  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant force\nthis weekend with triple digit heat during the afternoon hours\ntoday. The Extreme Heat Warning continues through 10pm this \nevening. \n\nSatellite showcases a large smoke plume stretched from eastern \nOregon across northern Montana. Visibility and air quality are\nlowering across the region but not quite low enough for head\nlines. \n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing through\nat least mid-week and possibly into the weekend with highs in the\n90s to around 100 degrees each day. Conditions will also be mostly\ndry, although there may be the occasional shortwave to trigger\nthunderstorms.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM Deviations include HRRR/RAP blends to enhance visibility \nreductions due to smoke through the day.",
